# Emulation of Micro:bit v2.0
# with application 001-LED-ON.s written in assembly language
# 20260928, Ondrej DURAS (+GoogleAI) NOKIA Public OpenWare GNU/GPLv2

# 1. creating emulation platform
using sysbus
mach create "ubit2-1"
#machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/cpus/nrf52840.repl
machine loadPlatformDescription $CWD/002-microbit_v2.repl

# following not needed anymore, becose microbit_v2.repl we customized now :-)
# decreasing memory on fly - chip changes from nRF52840 to nRF52833
# differences:
# nRF52833 Flash  512kB Ram 128kB
#sysbus.flash Size 0x100000
#sysbus.ram   Size 0x40000
# nRF52840 Flash 1024kB Ram 256kB
#sysbus.flash Size 0x80000
#sysbus.ram   Size 0x20000

# 2. starting WebUI for visualization
emulation CreateServer "http" 8080


# 3. loading application into platfomr FLASH memory
# sysbu LoadELF @00A-LED-ON.elf
sysbus LoadHEX @00A-LED-ON.hex


# 4. turning ledMatrix visualization ON
showAnalyzer sysbus.ledMatrix

# 5. Console setup
# PC, Opcode alebo PCAndOpcode
# cpu CreateExecutionTracing "tracer" @stdout PC
# text file where log is going to be written
#cpu CreateExecutionTracing "tracer" @trace.log PC
# ... in workspace
cpu CreateExecutionTracing "tracer" trace.log PC

# names of C functions directly visible in .log file
sysbus.cpu LogFunctionNames true

# after loading this use command
# start
# when you like to stop the simulation , then use command
# pause

# --- end ---

